  "description": "For each statement [SELECT `ID` FROM T9 ;; SELECT ID FROM `T9` ;; SELECT `ID` FROM `T9` ;; SELECT `Col Name` FROM `T Space` ;; SELECT [Col Name] FROM `T Space` ;; SELECT `Col Name` FROM [T Space] ;; SELECT t.`ID` FROM T9 AS t ;; SELECT `t`.ID FROM T9 AS t ;; SELECT ID AS `x y` FROM T9 ;; SELECT ID FROM T9 ORDER BY `ID`]: OpenRecordset as a snapshot and every row read. One element varies: where the backtick is (table, column, qualified column, alias, ORDER BY) and whether the name has a space. The fixture copy is opened read-only.",
